# The build context is the whole repository, because a portal compiles the shared packages from
# source. Everything below is either this machine's state or something that must never become an
# image layer.

# Dependencies are installed inside the image, from the lockfile. A Windows `node_modules` copied
# into a Linux image carries the wrong Prisma engines and the wrong native binaries, and the failure
# looks like a broken build rather than a wrong file.
**/node_modules

# Builds are produced by the image build.
**/.next
**/dist
**/out
**/storybook-static
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.turbo

# Secrets and machine-local configuration. `bun run verify` reads `apps/api/.env`; an image that
# baked it would carry a database password and a live SMTP login to every registry it was pushed to.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Uploaded bytes and the local database directory — runtime state, not source.
apps/api/storage
pgdata

# Repository machinery an image never runs.
.git
.github
design.md
HOURLOOM_BUILDING_PLAYBOOK.md
**/*.md
!README.md
!apps/site/content/**/*.md
!ARCHITECTURE.md
